doesn't this prove that what we're doing  up there is absolutely insane top gun  maverick is filled with incredible  stunts which of course you know by now  aren't cgi but did you know the stunts  were so dangerous they even had the real  aviators scared that's what topkin's  been doing for years making grown men  cry number one how could anybody say no  to tom cruise cruz is a licensed pilot  and he's flown a p-51 propeller-driven  fighter plane and some helicopters but  the navy denied him permission to fly an  f-18 fighter jet so that wasn't him  piloting the crazy stunts he was in the  back seat actually all of the actors  were and were doing their lines at the  same time director joseph kaczynski said  probably the most dangerous and daring  is in the middle of the film where  maverick flies the course to prove the  mission can be flown for that sequence  tom went through the real top gun  low-level training course at less than  50 feet above the ground at 500 miles  per hour the plane was so close to the  ground that it was stirring up dust and  making the cameras on the ground shake  aerial coordinator kevin larosa ii said  when you see them flying low over  terrain in between valleys dogfighting  that's really our cast  number two mountain stunts are stunning  unfortunately miles teller was stunned  in a different way when they go over a  mountain peak they don't go over like  this as soon as they get to the top they  go inverted well teller didn't strap  himself in tight enough and was lifted  out of his seat when the jet inverted he  hit his head against the canopy and that  shot made it into the final cut of the  film it's in the movie actually i hit my  head on the canopy and i thought it was  an unusable take not that they go  looking for mistakes to happen but when  they do they're unrepeatable gold  number three imagine having allergies  and being burned by tom cruise at the  same time poor teller wasn't having a  great time on set like sure flying in  airplanes is awesome but between hitting  his head and now blood poisoning he just  can't catch a break teller says we  landed and i'm just like man i'm not  feeling too good i was really hot and i  just started itching like crazy so i get  out of the jet and i'm just covered in  hives like head to toe instantly i go to  a doctor i do like a blood analysis this  that whatever i'm in an oatmeal bath at  night so he goes to tell crews about his  experience well tom it turns out  i have jet fuel in my blood and cruz's  response is  legendary tom just goes yeah i was born  with a kid it wasn't just jet fuel  though he also had flame retardant and  pesticides in his blood that flame  retardant should help with that sick  burn though number four on top of blood  poisoning and whacking his head teller  also wet himself okay not really but he  did have one moment in the f-18 hornet  jet where he thought he was a goner he  admitted there was a sequence where we  were heading straight towards the ground  and you do what's called a max g pull-up  you're heading down and at the last  second you yank up and it's really tough  for the pilot it's something they train  in all the time but it was the first  time we'd done a maneuver like that and  i completely stopped acting i looked at  the ground and thought this wasn't going  to end well for me  number five it's safe to say any stunt  in a plane is dangerous but this one is  pretty nerve-wracking they were actually  flying in the mountains with very little  room for error i mean the mountains are  less than 100 feet off each wing tip and  there's cloud cover sometimes too  number six just one of the many times  the actors would lose their lunch was  the upside-down shots but monica barbaro  was a natural at that due to her dance  training saying there was a funny moment  where a couple of the guys were saying  they hated going upside down and i was  like i've been going upside down forever  i would do handstands before flights it  helped me control some of the weird  feelings of blood rushing to spaces you  don't usually want it to number 7.  during monica's callback audition she  did a little oopsy and lied to the  director upon being asked if she was a  strong swimmer he's like can you swim i  was like yeah he was like you're a  comfortable swimmer i was like yeah you  know lying they all did a ton of swim  training just in case they needed to  eject over water but this is next level  water training the actors were being  pushed off a high rise and fell into a  pool and had to unstrap their parachutes  and there's one drill where the wind was  pushing the parachute across the water  man was monica ever in over her head  luckily she got to spend a ton of extra  time in the water training number eight  just imagine if this movie didn't get  made because tom couldn't be bothered to  put a helmet on we know it's a dorky  thought but seriously for somebody who's  so into health and safety on a plane he  kinda lets all that fly out the window  when it comes to his motorbike maybe  that's because bikes don't have windows  number nine the roof isn't on fire but  it isn't attached either in the opening  scene maverick flies over ed harris and  it rips the roof off of the shack thanks  to the force of the jet's takeoff watch  it rips the roof off the guard shack  that was not planned director kozinski  knew at that moment that there was no  need to rebuild the set because that  take was the only one they needed that  was a one-take thing where we destroyed  the set and that's the only shot we got  well that could have been a whole lot  more dangerous but luckily the roof  didn't fly too far  number 10. you've got to be prepared for  things to go wrong that's the difference  between an amateur and a pro so they did  a controlled stall where they turn off  the engine and you're free falling it  got pretty real pretty quick to be  honest with you number 11. training is  just controlled danger boot camp  training happened with the navy and the  top gun school to formulate how to shoot  the movie practically the actors started  out flying in single-engine airplanes to  build out their spatial awareness inside  the aircraft next they went in the l-39  and went and flew aerobatics to feel  what it's like in a jet tom cruise  developed the flight training program  that the actors needed to go through so  he designed a program that would get  them as ready as they could be the boot  camp took three months and the actors  had to develop skills in underwater  evacuation aerial aviation and flight  one thing in particular made these  flying scenes dangerous and that's the  dynamic pressure of the g-force that can  cause a lack of blood supply and make  pilots go unconscious kevin said i like  to attribute it to something similar to  muscle memory so it's a tolerance that  you build up and that's what paramount  and crews made with this pilot training  program to acclimate them and build up  the g-tolerance and build up their  fatigue levels without that there  wouldn't have been a movie in the  original top gun a stunt pilot named art  shoal fatefully plunged into the pacific  ocean after his pitts s2 camera plane  failed to recover from a spin he  suffered the same fate as the character  goose so when you're filming a sequel  with a history like that you'd better  take every precaution number 12 lots of  injuries sweat and vomit went into the  making of top gun actually tom cruise  was all too familiar with that geforce  feeling because in the first movie he  vomited in his helmet which is most  definitely why he did the boot camp  every minute of extreme motion sickness  while filming is money wasted before  cruz signed on to star in the original  top gun he took a test flight in a jet  he was flying at 6.5 g's and felt the  blood drain from his head he vomited in  his fighter pilot mask and he learned  from that to squeeze his thighs and abs  to stay conscious kevin said there's no  pulling over on the side of the road  when you're in a 50 000 pound fa-18  doing 500 knots in a canyon you're in it  let's be real pretty much everybody  except for the dancer vomited at least  once in the original movie and in the  sequel top gun maverick outdid itself  truly there were a ton of close calls  but we're just glad no one was injured  too bad for the sequel would you set  foot in an f-18 fighter jet given the  risks passenger or pilot let us know in  the comments and thanks for hanging out  with us here at the things

